BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Morehead Planetarium & Science Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260828T003000
DTSTAMP:20260821T221037
CREATED:20260720T192708Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260721T164830Z
UID:39912-1787866200-1787877000@moreheadplanetarium.org
SUMMARY:Skywatching & Show: Lunar Eclipse
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the lunar eclipse with Morehead’s astronomy educators!\n\n\n\nOn Thursday\, August 27\, celebrate the partial lunar eclipse with a special evening at Morehead Planetarium and Science Center! Under the climate-controlled\, always-clear planetarium sky\, we’ll simulate the eclipse\, tour the North Carolina night sky\, and take a spectacular journey through our universe. If the weather permits\, join us after the show for eclipse observing from the Morehead Sundial.  \n\n\n\nSchedule\n\n\n\n9:30 – 10:30 PM | Carolina Skies: Lunar Eclipse show \n\n\n\n10:30 PM – 12:30 AM | Free skywatching (weather permitting) \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTickets for Carolina Skies: Lunar Eclipse are available starting on Monday\, July 27. UNC-Chapel Hill students can enjoy $6 tickets to the planetarium show. Log in to Heel Life to receive your student discount code! \n\n\n\n\nCarolina Skies tickets\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBefore You Go: Helpful Tips & Important Details\n\n\n\nTo make the most of your evening under the stars\, we suggest bringing a cozy blanket or some chairs. For everyone’s safety and enjoyment\, we kindly ask that you leave your pets at home\, even if they’re on a leash. The combination of darkness\, crowds\, expensive telescopes\, and pets isn’t ideal\, and pets won’t be allowed near the telescopes. \n\n\n\nPlease note that this event is weather-dependent. In the event of a cancellation\, we will provide updates on our website and social media. We can’t wait to share the wonders of the night sky with you! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHave more questions about skywatching? Visit our FAQs page!  \n\n\n\n\nSkywatching FAQs
URL:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/calendar/skywatching-lunar-eclipse/
LOCATION:Morehead Planetarium and Science Center\, 250 E Franklin St\, Chapel Hill\, North Carolina\, 27516\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/yu-kato-ZOSkWlDVCsE-unsplash.jpg
END:VEVENT
