BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Morehead Planetarium & Science Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260829T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260829T150000
DTSTAMP:20260821T221037
CREATED:20260812T172035Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260820T230315Z
UID:40148-1788001200-1788015600@moreheadplanetarium.org
SUMMARY:Saturday Science Sparks: Warmer Climates
DESCRIPTION:The Heat is on…and the Science is Cool! \n\n\n\nScientists are building tools to help people and the planet deal with hotter days. Join members of UNC’s Data-Driven EnviroLab (DDL) for a fire hands-on experience around the challenge of a warmer climate!  \n\n\n\nYou can meet members of DDL in the Launch Lab from 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. All ages welcome. This special program is included in admission. \n\n\n\n\n\nAbout the Data-Driven EnviroLab\n\n\n\nThe Data-Driven EnviroLab is an interdisciplinary research collective at UNC-Chapel Hill that uses data and technology to address pressing environmental challenges. Led by Associate Professor Angel Hsu\, DDL transforms complex datasets into actionable insights that inform policy\, promote accountability\, and support equitable\, evidence-based solutions worldwide. \n\n\n\nMORE is happening at Morehead this year\n\n\n\nNew for 2026\, Saturday Science Sparks offers Morehead guests a closer encounter with current science. Covering topics like astronomy\, the physics of juggling\, and computer science\, this program collaborates with community partners and academic clubs\, bringing you up-close experiences in the exciting world of STEAM. Saturday Science Sparks is open to the public and included in admission.
URL:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/calendar/saturday-science-sparks-warmer-climates/
LOCATION:Morehead Planetarium and Science Center\, 250 E Franklin St\, Chapel Hill\, North Carolina\, 27516\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2026-August29-ScienceSparks-DDL-04.jpg
END:VEVENT
